{{Character|title1 = Hero|activity = Pick up the Gun and Kill the [[Murderer]]|image1=[[File:HeroText.png|center|frameless|150px]]|win_theme=[[File:Sherrif Win.mp3|center|frameless]]}}'''Hero''' is a non-chosen role in [[Murder Mystery 2]]. Their [[Roles|role]] initially as an [[Innocent]] is to pick up the killed [[Sheriff|Sheriff's]] and previous Hero's gun, and then work with the other Innocents to find out who the [[Murderer]] is and successfully shoot them before the round ends.
==Controls==

=== PC===

* Press 1 to equip the gun.
*Move mouse to aim your crosshair on someone.
*Left-click to shoot.

===Mobile (phone) ===

* Press equip button or tap the gun in your inventory to equip it.
*Tap a person to shoot them.

=== Mobile (tablet)===

*Press equip button or tap gun in your inventory to equip it.
*In third person, tap someone to shoot them.
*In first person, swipe the crosshair on someone, let go of it, and then tap the person to shoot.

===Xbox (Doesn't work on PS4 Bluetooth Controller)===

* Press LB to equip the gun.
*Crosshair does not move, so to aim, move RS to position the crosshair properly on a person.
* Press RT to shoot.
==Trivia==
* There can be as many Heros as there are Innocents.
* The Hero and Sheriff cannot be on the map at the same time. The Sheriff has to die in order for an Innocent to become a Hero.
*If a Sheriff resets or dies by any means at the beginning 10 seconds of the game, the dropped gun can be picked up and used before the 10-second cooldown is over.
*There is a glitch in which if both the Murderer gets shot and the Hero gets stabbed/a knife thrown at them at the same time, it will reveal the results, but both player icons in the results will be marked with an X, but it'll mark the Hero as the winner.
*The two guns in the "VICTORY!" frame are unevenly aligned.
*If a Hero shoots an Innocent, both of them will die.
*If a Hero leaves the game, the weapon will spawn somewhere on the map.
** The weapon used to disappear from the round completely, making the round much easier for the murderer.
*If a Hero successfully shoots the Murderer, it will count towards their Innocent survivals.
*It is commonly believed that the Hero win theme is from a song called "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abPoaHdHXRg I Respect You]". This is not true.
*The win theme for the Hero was made in GarageBand.
**It was made with the Above and Beyond Synth, and Almost Electro Beat.

